    scenarioBiasEn: 'The driver trusted the digital map over their physical eyes and local weather alerts, committing the classic Map-Territory fallacy.',
    scenarioOptimalEn: 'Always treat models as advisory hints: verify current ground truth with physical observation before taking irreversible actions.',
    scenarioReflectionEn: 'What dashboard metric or performance review score do you optimize for at work that doesn’t actually reflect the real quality of your contribution?',
    howToRecognizeEn: 'Arguing that reality "must be wrong" because your theory, policy document, or financial spreadsheet predicted otherwise.',
    whereEn: 'Macroeconomic policy, algorithmic trading, corporate OKRs/KPIs, military combat operations, and AI prompt engineering.',
    misconceptionsEn: 'Myth: "Because maps are imperfect, we should discard all models and rely purely on gut instinct." Fact: Models are indispensable tools for navigation; we must simply remember their boundary conditions and margins of error.',
    limitationsEn: 'In purely closed mathematical systems (like Euclidean geometry or chess), the rules and axioms ARE the complete territory; the fallacy applies to physical and human systems.',
    howToRespondEn: 'The Ground-Truth Audit: Step out of the boardroom or terminal and spend 4 hours observing actual customers using your product in the real world.',
